1
00:03:25,714 --> 00:03:31,714
The Riven is a drama film directed by Michael Fredianelli.

2
00:06:51,428 --> 00:06:57,428
College freshman Selena Sutter (Samantha Koerner) gets more than she bargains for when her new
roommate Amy (Jess Chanliau) unwillingly drags her to a raucous frat party.

3
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
Left to her own devices, Selena ends up shattered by a vicious attack and is left to
finish her academic year with a crippling affliction and little hope.

4
00:13:42,857 --> 00:13:48,857
With the help of an intuitive science professor, she begins to heal and open her heart to an unexpected
romance with a friendly teacher's assistant (Josiah Frampton), who may be hiding a secret from her.

5
00:17:08,571 --> 00:17:14,571
But struggling with a shaky past and the abrupt return of her assailant,
Selena's new questionable affair may only contribute to her downfall.

6
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
Selena Sutter, played by Samantha Koerner.

7
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Eric Bateman, played by Josiah Frampton.

8
00:27:25,714 --> 00:27:31,714
Amy Mason, played by Jess Chanliau.

9
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Matthew Smith, played by Bret Grantham.

10
00:34:17,142 --> 00:34:23,142
Mr. Sullivan, played by Jeremy Koerner.

11
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Stephen Sutter, played by Ray Medved.

12
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Riven: The Sequel to Myst is a 1997 adventure game developed by Cyan Productions and
published by Red Orb Entertainment for Mac OS and Microsoft Windows.

13
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
It is the sequel to 1993's Myst, and the second installment of the Myst series.

14
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The game's story is set after the events of its predecessor; having rescued Atrus, who had been trapped by his
sons, the player character is enlisted by him to free his wife from his power-hungry father, Gehn.

15
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Riven takes place almost entirely on the Age of Riven, a world
slowly falling apart due to Gehn's destructive rule.

16
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
Development of Riven began soon after Myst became a
success, and spanned more than three years.

17
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
In an effort to create a visual style distinct from that of Myst, director Robyn Miller and his brother,
producer Rand Miller, recruited production designer Richard Vander Wende as a co-director.

18
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Broderbund employed a multimillion-dollar advertising
campaign to publicize the game's release.

19
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
Riven received ports to the PlayStation, Sega
Saturn, Pocket PC, iOS and Android.

20
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Riven was praised by reviewers, with the magazine Salon
proclaiming that the game approaches the level of art.

21
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Critics positively noted the puzzles and immersive experience of the gameplay, though publications
such as Edge felt that the nature of point-and-click gameplay limited the title heavily.

22
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The best-selling game of 1997, Riven sold 1.5 million copies in one year.

23
01:18:51,428 --> 01:18:57,428
After the game's release, Robyn Miller left Cyan to form his own development
studio, ending the professional partnership of the two brothers.

24
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
Rand stayed at Cyan and continued to work on Myst-related products including The
Myst Reader and the real-time rendered game Uru: Ages Beyond Myst.

25
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
The next entry in the Myst series, Myst III: Exile, was
developed by Presto Studios and published by Ubisoft.

26
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
A remake of the game, recreating the world in fully explorable 3D and supporting
both flatscreen and virtual reality modes, was released in June 2024.

27
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The tone is emotional.
